class.description:
A script written in [url=https://github.com/hemlang/hemlock]Hemlock[/url], saved with the [code].hml[/code] extension and run by Hemlock's embedded interpreter.
The whole file is the script. Its top level runs once per instance, when the script is attached to an object, so top-level [code]let[/code] variables hold per-object state and top-level [code]fn[/code] functions are its methods, including the engine callbacks ([code]_ready[/code], [code]_process(delta)[/code], [code]_notification(what)[/code], ...). [code]export let[/code] makes a variable an inspector property. [code]owner[/code] is the object the instance belongs to, and [code]godot[/code] holds the engine helpers.
Three optional top-level constants configure the script. They are read without running it, and each must be a literal: [code]const EXTENDS = "Node2D";[/code] names the native class the script attaches to (default [code]Object[/code]), [code]const TOOL = true;[/code] runs it in the editor, and [code]const SIGNALS = ["hit"];[/code] declares signals.
[codeblock lang=text]
const EXTENDS = "Node2D";

export let speed: f64 = 120.0;

fn _process(delta) {
    let p = owner.get("position");
    owner.set("position", godot.vec2(p.x + speed * delta, p.y));
}
[/codeblock]
